INT. CONVERTED BOWLING ALLEY COURTROOM - DAY

Lane six has been boarded over to serve as the well of the court. The bench is a ball return with a raised platform. Pins are painted on the wall behind the jury box.

JUDGE KOWALCZYK, sixties, stocky, in robes over a polo shirt, taps a gavel made from a bowling pin. At the plaintiff's table, ATTORNEY SEUN ADEBAYO, thirties, stands with a legal pad. At the defence table, ATTORNEY GRACE PELLETIER, forties, fidgets with a pen. In the witness chair, an UNKNOWN WITNESS in a lab coat waits. By the door, BAILIFF GUS, twenties, eats sunflower seeds.

ADEBAYO
Please state your name for the record.

WITNESS
I am a forensic engineer.

ADEBAYO
Your name.

PELLETIER
Objection. Asked and not answered.

KOWALCZYK
Overruled. Let her finish.

WITNESS
Dr. Isolde Varga.

ADEBAYO
Dr. Varga, did you inspect the lane that night?

VARGA
I did. The oil pattern was uneven by almost four feet.

PELLETIER
Objection, speculation.

KOWALCZYK
It's her job, counsel. Sit down.

PELLETIER
Your Honor-

ADEBAYO
She measured it, Your Honor, she didn't guess.

KOWALCZYK
I said sit down.

GUS
(muttering)
Strike.

KOWALCZYK
Bailiff!

GUS
Sorry, sir. Habit.

VARGA
May I continue?

ADEBAYO
Please.

PELLETIER
Objection!

KOWALCZYK
Overruled. Overruled. All of it. Go.

VARGA
The pattern was consistent with deliberate tampering.

A silence. Pelletier drops her pen. It rolls across the floor and into the gutter.

KOWALCZYK
Well. That's a spare.
